  "data": {
    "body": "A block of mass $M_A$ = \\textbf{2 kg} and specific heat $C_A$ has an initial temperature of $T_A$. It is brought into thermal contact with a second block of mass $M_B$ = \\textbf{10 kg} and specific heat $C_B$ at initial temperature $T_B$. When the two blocks have come to equilibrium, they are at temperature \\textbf{T}. Block A's temperature has changed by $\\mid \\triangle T_A \\mid$ = \\textbf{6 K} while block B's temperature has changed by $\\mid \\triangle T_B \\mid$ = \\textbf{9 K}.\n\nWhat is the value of the \\textbf{ratio of specific heats}, $\\frac{C_A}{C_B}$? \\textbf{Select the closest answer.}",
